From 2912965c2f94ae30b1b392ed52a9c28ffbbff188 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:41:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Match the memory pool prototype to its implementation

wgmempool_Init takes a size_t block size. Its private header declares a
32-bit argument, causing incompatible calls on LP64 targets and a type
mismatch at link time with GCC LTO. Use size_t in the declaration.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Upstream-Reference: https://github.com/LibreOffice/libexttextcat/blob/4872bb3ee1e47b076517dc0787cee5215aa34f60/src/wg_mempool.c#L86
Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
 src/wg_mempool.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/wg_mempool.h b/src/wg_mempool.h
index 1041a84..4702c04 100644
--- a/src/wg_mempool.h
+++ b/src/wg_mempool.h
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@ extern "C"
      * mempool handler on success, NULL on error.
      * 
      */
-    extern void *wgmempool_Init(uint4 blocksize, size_t maxstrsize);
+    extern void *wgmempool_Init(size_t blocksize, size_t maxstrsize);
 
 
     /* 
